Project Overview

The Personalized AI Tutor is a Generative AI-based learning application designed to provide curriculum-aligned educational assistance to students in Classes 8–10. It uses Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) to retrieve relevant information from educational PDF documents and generate context-aware answers to students' questions.
The system also incorporates an adaptive learning mechanism that tracks student performance, identifies weak topics, and adjusts question difficulty based on learning progress.

Key Features
Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG): Retrieves relevant educational content before generating answers.
Semantic Search: Uses Sentence Transformers to understand questions and retrieve relevant text.
Vector Search: Implements FAISS for efficient similarity-based document retrieval.
AI-Based Answer Generation: Uses FLAN-T5 Large to generate context-aware responses.
Adaptive Learning: Adjusts learning difficulty based on student performance.
Performance Tracking: Monitors student accuracy, attempts, and weak topics.
PDF Processing: Extracts, cleans, and splits educational documents into smaller text chunks.
Interactive Interface: Uses Streamlit for the learning application.

